# Transcrypt: these files are stored encrypted in git and stay plaintext in the
# working tree. A fresh clone reads them as base64 until it is unlocked with the
# shared key — see "Encrypted files" in CLAUDE.md.
#
# The `text=auto eol=lf` on each rule below normalizes the base64 ciphertext on the way into the blob, which
# is what stops a Windows clone and a macOS clone re-encrypting each other's commits forever. Never replace
# it with `-text`, and do not drop it to match upstream's bare line — upstream has no Windows story.

*.secret.* filter=crypt diff=crypt merge=crypt text=auto eol=lf

# The track-achievements skill is encrypted whole rather than per-file: Claude
# Code discovers a skill by its literal SKILL.md name, so the entry point cannot
# carry the *.secret.* marker.
.claude/skills/track-achievements/** filter=crypt diff=crypt merge=crypt text=auto eol=lf
